t/issues/100387","id":2572016947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZTd0z","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T02:02:47Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T02:03:02Z","body":"> I think you could change [this line](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/dc5f1b7a2826962f02230227abc486ac160ae66c/editor/editor_settings.cpp#L596) to give it a different default, but I don't know what the underlying problem is interfacing with the filesystem. I haven't made one of these before so hopefully this is helpful. 😃\n\nThat setting didn't change between 4.3.stable and 4.4.dev, so I'm surprised you're only encountering the issue on 4.4.dev. Are you sure this is not because you set different values (editor settings are stored per minor version since 4.3)?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2572016947/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2597395682","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100387#issuecomment-2597395682","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100387","id":2597395682,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a0Rzi","user":{"login":"peerlessblue","id":113931066,"node_id":"U_kgDOBspzOg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113931066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue","html_url":"https://github.com/peerlessblue","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-17T04:10:25Z","updated_at":"2025-01-17T04:10:25Z","body":"> > I think you could change [this line](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/dc5f1b7a2826962f02230227abc486ac160ae66c/editor/editor_settings.cpp#L596) to give it a different default, but I don't know what the underlying problem is interfacing with the filesystem. I haven't made one of these before so hopefully this is helpful. 😃\n> \n> That setting didn't change between 4.3.stable and 4.4.dev, so I'm surprised you're only encountering the issue on 4.4.dev. Are you sure this is not because you set different values (editor settings are stored per minor version since 4.3)?\n\nI'm not saying that setting caused the issue, I'm saying that changing it to a different default could avoid the issue until the underlying cause is identified and fixed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2597395682/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616658801","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100387#issuecomment-2616658801","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100387","id":2616658801,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b9wtx","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T19:03:29Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T19:03:29Z","body":"> This is particularly problematic because Godot's default project directory, C:/Users/username/OneDrive/Documents, is synchronized with OneDrive by default.\n\nOn most Windows installs, it is not. Godot is using whatever OS have configured as default \"Documents\" folder, so changing it is not a good way to solve this. We can't hardcode some other value since we can't know if it exists, and the result will be unexpected for a lot of users (I do not think a lot of people will prefer `c:\\` root as default, and it's usually not writable by non-admin users).\n\nYou can already override default path in the editor settings (`filesystem/directories/default_project_path`).\n\n> Godot will become unresponsive and attempt to download from OneDrive if there are files in the root of the directory that are not stored on-device immediately on opening the file picker in order to open an existing project.\n\nNot sure what's the difference between 4.3 and 4.4. I'll try bisecting it, if I can reproduce it. But this is likely true for any slow network drive and on any OS, not just OneDrive, so it might be worth making file list update threaded.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616658801/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645522369","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100387#issuecomment-2645522369","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100387","id":2645522369,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dr3fB","user":{"login":"peerlessblue","id":113931066,"node_id":"U_kgDOBspzOg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113931066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue","html_url":"https://github.com/peerlessblue","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peerlessblue/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-08T13:05:12Z","updated_at":"2025-02-08T13:05:12Z","body":"> > This is particularly problematic because Godot's default project directory, C:/Users/username/OneDrive/Documents, is synchronized with OneDrive by default.\n> \n> On most Windows installs, it is not. Godot is using whatever OS have configured as default \"Documents\" folder, so changing it is not a good way to solve this. We can't hardcode some other value since we can't know if it exists, and the result will be unexpected for a lot of users (I do not think a lot of people will prefer `c:\\` root as default, and it's usually not writable by non-admin users).\n> \n> You can already override default path in the editor settings (`filesystem/directories/default_project_path`).\n> \n> > Godot will become unresponsive and attempt to download from OneDrive if there are files in the root of the directory that are not stored on-device immediately on opening the file picker in order to open an existing project.\n> \n> Not sure what's the difference between 4.3 and 4.4. I'll try bisecting it, if I can reproduce it. But this is likely true for any slow network drive and on any OS, not just OneDrive, so it might be worth making file list update threaded.\n\nI'm not sure what you mean by \"most installs it is not\", because having OneDrive sync My Documents is encouraged at Windows installation.\n\nThe fundamental problem is that it's choking on what I presume to be symbolic links. Improving the performance of populating the list won't solve the issue because it does _something_ that is forcing OneDrive to download every file, which might not even be possible. It shouldn't be doing this. The performance on builds without the bug is fine.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645522369/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2663658822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100387#issuecomment-2663658822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100387","id":2663658822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6exDVG","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-17T16:59:25Z","updated_at":"2025-02-17T16:59:25Z","body":"Can anyone on the Review Release Channel of Windows 11 try installing update [KB5052094](https://blogs.windows.com/windows-insider/2025/02/13/releasing-windows-11-build-22631-4969-to-the-release-preview-channel/)? It's said to fix the issue according to [this article](https://www.pcgamer.com/software/operating-systems/about-darn-time-microsoft-says-it-has-fixed-the-annoying-lag-in-windows-explorer-when-working-with-cloud-based-files/).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2663658822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2705213283","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100387#issuecomment-2705213283","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100387","id":2705213283,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hPkdj","user":{"login":"ryanttb","id":258962,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1ODk2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanttb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanttb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T00:06:54Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T00:06:54Z","body":"This issue is different. Godot 4.4 actually _downloads_ all the cloud files locally before returning to being responsive. This did not happen with Godot 4.3.\n\nI'm on Windows 10 and can right-click on a cloud-only OneDrive file in Explorer and get Properties without causing a download of the fil